Optional last resort for future bugs: `process.on('uncaughtException', (e) => { console.error('[fatal]', e); store.flush(); process.exit(1); });` so a crash still flushes favorites/groups/stats before Fly restarts the process.

```kotlin
override fun onClosing(webSocket: WebSocket, code: Int, reason: String) {
    webSocket.close(1000, null)   // termine la poignée de main de fermeture
    Hub.main.post { if (webSocket === ws) onSocketClosed() }
}
```
and make the heartbeat independent of OkHttp callbacks:
```kotlin
private val heartbeatRunnable = Runnable {
    if (ws != null) { dropSocket(); onSocketClosed() }   // on relance nous-mêmes la reconnexion
}
```
dropSocket() nulls `ws`, so the old socket's later onClosed/onFailure are ignored by the existing `webSocket === ws` guard (no double reconnect).

```js
