```
Use `clientIp(req)` at line 70. Add a global upstream budget independent of IPs (fixed 60 s window, e.g. 120 Google fetches/min, beyond → 503 'tts busy'), checked right before the upstream fetch. Optional: sign ttsUrl in ttsUrlFor (`&sig=` + first 16 hex of HMAC(LINK_SECRET, text)) and exempt valid signatures from the per-IP limit; clients treat ttsUrl as opaque, so this is wire-compatible (only replays of pre-change history entries would be unsigned).

```js
const ttsInflight = new Map();   // clé -> Promise<Buffer>
function getTtsAudio(lang, text) {
  const key = `${lang}|${text}`;
  const hit = ttsCache.get(key);
  if (hit) { ttsCache.delete(key); ttsCache.set(key, hit); return Promise.resolve(hit); }
  if (!ttsInflight.has(key)) ttsInflight.set(key, (async () => {
    // même URL Google et même User-Agent qu'aujourd'hui
    const g = await fetch(googleTtsUrl(lang, text), { headers: TTS_HEADERS, signal: AbortSignal.timeout(8000) });
    if (!g.ok) throw new Error(`upstream ${g.status}`);
    const buf = Buffer.from(await g.arrayBuffer());
    ttsCache.set(key, buf);
    if (ttsCache.size > TTS_CACHE_MAX) ttsCache.delete(ttsCache.keys().next().value);
    return buf;
  })().finally(() => ttsInflight.delete(key)));
  return ttsInflight.get(key);
}
```
handleTts: if cached or `ttsInflight.has(key)` → `sendTtsAudio(res, await getTtsAudio(lang, text))` without the rate limit; else rate-limit, then the same; catch → 502 as today. Warm-up: when a drop with tts reaches ≥1 overlay, call `getTtsAudio('fr', payload.tts).catch(() => {})` (ttsUrlFor sends no lang → 'fr'; payload.tts is trimmed and ≤200, so keys match). Fix comment 20-21.

