```js
// Envoie un drop aux cibles joignables ; renvoie les noms livrés / non joignables.
function deliverDrop(senderId, guildId, channelId, targets, payload) {
  const delivered = [], notReachable = [];
  let raw = null;
  for (const t of targets) {
    if (!canDrop(senderId, t.id, guildId)) { notReachable.push(t.username); continue; }
    raw ??= JSON.stringify(payload);
    userLinks.get(t.id).ws.send(raw);   // multi-appareils : chaque socket ouverte
    delivered.push(t.username);
    bumpStats(senderId, t.id, false);   // sans persistStore
  }
  if (delivered.length) { persistStore(); registerDropForReactions(payload, senderId, channelId); }
  return { delivered, notReachable };
}
```
bumpStats gets a `persist = true` parameter. dispatchToTargets keeps only the reply formatting on top of deliverDrop(interaction.user.id, interaction.guildId, interaction.channelId, targets, payload); the delayed timer sets payload.ts then calls deliverDrop(senderId, guildId, channelId, targets, payload); /dropall passes `recipients.map(r => ({ id: r.userId, username: r.username }))` and formats its reply from `delivered`.

```js
const LINK_FAIL_WINDOW_MS = 10 * 60_000, LINK_FAIL_MAX = 5;
const linkFails = new Map();   // userId -> { count, since }
function linkLocked(uid) { const f = linkFails.get(uid); return !!f && Date.now() - f.since < LINK_FAIL_WINDOW_MS && f.count >= LINK_FAIL_MAX; }
function noteLinkFail(uid) { const f = linkFails.get(uid); if (!f || Date.now() - f.since >= LINK_FAIL_WINDOW_MS) linkFails.set(uid, { count: 1, since: Date.now() }); else f.count++; }
```
Top of case 'link': `if (linkLocked(uid)) return interaction.reply({ content: '⏱️ Trop de codes invalides — réessaie dans quelques minutes.', flags: MessageFlags.Ephemeral });`. Call noteLinkFail on the 'belongs to another user' reply and both 'Invalid or expired code' replies; prune expired entries in an existing 5-min sweep. Optional: rotate pending codes every ~15 min (delete the old pendingOverlays entry first, then reissuePairingCode; both clients already show a new pairing_code while unlinked).

